# `TZ` and segmentation fault

The default `ld-linux.so` will, mysteriously, write to its own `RELRO` field that causes segfault when `TZ` is not set or `TZ=:/etc/localtime`.

The code that triggers this error is:

```c

void
__tzfile_read (const char *file, size_t extra, char **extrap)
{
  /* ... */
 read_again:
  if (__builtin_expect (__fread_unlocked ((void *) &tzhead, sizeof (tzhead), /* <- __fread_unlocked */
					  1, f) != 1, 0)
      || memcmp (tzhead.tzh_magic, TZ_MAGIC, sizeof (tzhead.tzh_magic)) != 0)
    goto lose;

}
```

The minimal reproducible case is `tests/guest/func/stdio_seek_read_smoke.c`.
